  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I'm currently using multiple WAN network to connect to the internet (round-robin enabled). Thus, my IP address is not so \"sticky\" compared to other setup without MultiWAN. If a network socket is closed and re-opened, there is a 66% chance the new socket will use a different IP address compared to the previous one. \nThe problem is, VRChat (game and its website) invalidates session when I used session from one IP address in another one. This results without disabling MultiWAN setup in my network, I cannot properly connect and play the game nor use the web interface.\n I know my setup is very uncommon among the users, but I'll really be glad if this game properly supports MultiWAN environment (give some option to keep the session between different IP addresses, or any other way).",
